<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Material Availability
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>A Note on Imports and Reskinning
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading1>Chapter 3: Crafting, Repair & the Working Economy
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>What This Chapter Covers
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>The Crafting Loop
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>GM Tuning: The Grit Knob
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>The material fraction is the single most powerful lever a GM has for adjusting the feel of the economy. The book defaults to 25% <0x2014> crafting is hard but workable. Raise it to 30% for a grittier setting where margins are tight and one bad month can ruin a shop. Raise it to 35% for a genuinely punishing economy where only masters in large cities can make it work. Lower it to 20% for a forgiving, high-fantasy economy where crafting is a reliable livelihood.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>No other parameter shifts the math as cleanly. Adjust this one first, and leave the rest at book defaults unless you have a specific reason to tune them.
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
