<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Bows
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Crossbows
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Thrown Weapons and Slings
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Ammunition Variants
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Historical Curiosities
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>The Slur (Bullet-Bow)
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A specialized crossbow with a split string and a small pouch rather than a bolt-groove, designed to fire lead pellets or stones. Used for hunting small game silently <0x2014> the pellet exits the weapon with almost no sound <0x2014> and for non-lethal crowd dispersal in some urban watch units.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Damage:<CharStyle:> Solid · <CharStyle:Bold>Range:<CharStyle:> Short · <CharStyle:Bold>Weight:<CharStyle:> 4 lbs · <CharStyle:Bold>Cost:<CharStyle:> 110 gp
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Traits:<CharStyle:> Silent release. Slight Stun bonus (high knockdown). Cannot fire standard bolts.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>The Multi-Bolt Organ Crossbow
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A theoretical siege defense weapon: five to seven crossbow prods mounted on a common frame with a shared trigger bar. Fires a spread of bolts in a five-foot arc. Historically never proved reliable <0x2014> the tension was impossible to balance across prods, and the machines typically failed within three firings.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Damage:<CharStyle:> Solid per bolt · <CharStyle:Bold>Range:<CharStyle:> Short · <CharStyle:Bold>Weight:<CharStyle:> 40 lbs (fixed mount) · <CharStyle:Bold>Cost:<CharStyle:> 500 gp
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Traits:<CharStyle:> Fires 1d4 bolts on each shot. On a natural failure, the frame cracks and the weapon is destroyed. Reload time: 5 rounds per bolt set.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>The Spring-Flinger (Hand Ballista)
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A portable torsion-powered launcher, hand-cranked and carried by two people. Hurls fire-pots, stones, or alchemical flasks. A weapon for defending a window or tower rather than an open field.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Damage:<CharStyle:> Crushing (plus alchemical or fire effects per payload) · <CharStyle:Bold>Range:<CharStyle:> Medium · <CharStyle:Bold>Weight:<CharStyle:> 35 lbs · <CharStyle:Bold>Cost:<CharStyle:> 450 gp
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Traits:<CharStyle:> Two-person crew. Torsion ropes fail in freezing weather (Moderate Durability penalty and fouling risk).
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>The Blowpipe
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A hollow tube, three to five feet long, through which small darts are launched by breath. Silent, short-ranged, and almost never lethal on its own <0x2014> but the ideal delivery mechanism for contact poisons.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Damage:<CharStyle:> Glancing (darts themselves) · <CharStyle:Bold>Range:<CharStyle:> Close · <CharStyle:Bold>Weight:<CharStyle:> 1 lb · <CharStyle:Bold>Cost:<CharStyle:> 25 gp
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Traits:<CharStyle:> Silent. Darts hold one dose of contact poison each (see Chapter 16). Slight Stealth bonus when carried disguised as a walking-stick.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>The Yumi (Asymmetric Bow)
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A Japanese longbow in which the grip is positioned below the center, producing an asymmetric shape. Designed for use from horseback and from a kneeling position, where the lower limb would not strike the ground or saddle.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Damage:<CharStyle:> Heavy · <CharStyle:Bold>Range:<CharStyle:> Long · <CharStyle:Bold>Weight:<CharStyle:> 2.5 lbs · <CharStyle:Bold>Cost:<CharStyle:> 200 gp
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Traits:<CharStyle:> Two-Handed. No penalty when fired from horseback, from a kneeling position, or from a crouching position. Moderate penalty in standard standing archery (wielder trained in yumi method is less accustomed to the conventional stance).
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Fantasy Variants
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Elven Moon-Silver Bow
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A bow of moon-silver with silver bowstring, granting all silver properties (bypasses lycanthrope resistance). The arrows fired from this bow gain silver properties for the duration of flight. Range is extended by one band (Long becomes Extreme). Cost: +Severe (×10) over base bow.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Dragon-Bone Crossbow
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A hand or light crossbow with a dragon-bone prod rather than wood or steel. Slight damage bonus and Major weight reduction. Carries the elemental affinity of the source dragon <0x2014> bolts fired from a fire-drake crossbow add Slight fire damage, etc. Cost: +Severe over base crossbow.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Rune-Bound Ammunition
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>Individual arrows or bolts can be rune-bound with minor effects (see Chapter 19). A rune-bound ignition arrow always ignites on impact even in rain; a rune-bound silver bolt carries silver's properties without requiring a silver warhead; a rune-bound piercing arrow gains a full Armor-Crack bonus. Cost: +Major per arrow for standard runes, +Severe for advanced. Most characters cannot afford rune-bound ammunition by the quiver; a handful of special arrows for critical shots is the normal usage pattern.
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Using Ranged Weapons in Specific Situations
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Maintenance
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
