<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Fantasy Variants
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Faye-touched Steeds
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>Some settings feature horses bred or blessed by fae powers <0x2014> horses that do not tire, that run on water, that appear only by moonlight. Treat as a courser or destrier with Moderate bonus to all Endurance rolls, immunity to mundane fear, and a Severe price bonus. Specific lore varies by setting; the mechanical profile does not.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Draconic Mounts
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A young dragon, a drake, or a wyvern may be tamed by appropriate characters in some settings. Treat as a giant flying mount with flight speed, a breath weapon (see Chapter 16 for elemental effects, multiplied by ×3 damage), and intelligence that often exceeds the rider's. Price: not applicable; dragons are not bought. See Chapter 19 for how to build this relationship mechanically.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Living-Wood Treants
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A moving tree-creature mount, rare and specific to druidic traditions. Extremely slow (half walking character speed), but can pass through dense forest without penalty and can heal itself overnight. Carry: 400 lbs. Not commercially available.
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
