<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading1>Chapter 11: Ships & Nautical Warfare
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>What This Chapter Covers
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>How Ships Are Stated
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>River and Coastal Craft
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Sea-Going Sailing Vessels
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>War Galleys and Rowing Vessels
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Specialty Vessels
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Fantasy Variants
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Elven Living-Wood Ship
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A ship built from living wood (Chapter 2), self-repairing and resistant to rot. Cannot be set alight by mundane fire. Durability increases by a Major bonus; repair happens overnight as long as the ship is afloat in clean water. Cost: +Severe (×10) over the base ship's price. Elves rarely sell ships; acquiring one is a major story event.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Sky-Ship (Aetheric Vessel)
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A rare class of flying vessel, powered by bound elementals, enchanted lifting crystals, or similar exotic principles. Specific lore varies wildly by setting. Treat as a sailing ship that moves at standard naval speed but through air rather than water. Vulnerable to very different threats (air currents, aerial predators, altitude limits). Cost: 50,000+ gp and almost always uniquely commissioned.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Ghost Ship
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A cursed or haunted vessel, sailed by the dead or controlled by a bound spirit. Mechanics vary entirely by setting; some provide otherwise-impossible capabilities (sailing without wind, vanishing into fog) in exchange for supernatural risks (the captain's soul, sanity of the crew, attraction of certain undead). Plot device rather than purchasable gear.
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
