<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading1>Chapter 13: Firearms & Artillery
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Gunpowder and the Changing Battlefield
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>The Misfire Problem
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Class
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Dry Conditions
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Damp
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Rain/Snow
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Hand cannon (early)
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>15%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>30%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>60%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Matchlock
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>10%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>25%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>60%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Wheellock
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>5%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>10%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>25%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Flintlock
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>3%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>8%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>20%
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Roll
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Outcome
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>1<0x2013>70
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Dud. Weapon fails to fire. Reload required.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>71<0x2013>90
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Pan-flash / smoke. No ball fired; shooter momentarily blind (Slight penalty, 1 round).
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>91<0x2013>97
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Slow fire. Shot fires on next round instead of this one.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>98<0x2013>99
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Barrel fouling. Weapon cannot fire until cleaned (10 minutes).
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>100
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Barrel burst. Weapon destroyed; shooter takes Heavy damage to firing hand.
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Personal Firearms
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Artillery
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Ammunition and Powder
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Historical Curiosities
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>The Puckle Gun
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>An 18th-century experimental multi-shot firearm with a rotating cylinder magazine. The Puckle Gun famously included square bullets for shooting Muslims and round bullets for shooting Christians. Impressive as an engineering curiosity, unreliable in practice, and nearly never fielded.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Damage:<CharStyle:> Solid (one shot per cylinder chamber; 9 chambers) · <CharStyle:Bold>Cost:<CharStyle:> 2,000 gp · <CharStyle:Bold>Weight:<CharStyle:> 40 lbs
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Traits:<CharStyle:> Mounted weapon. Rotating cylinder <0x2014> fires 9 shots before reload (20 minutes). Misfire rate 15% per shot.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>The Flash Bomb
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A small thrown clay pot filled with black powder, a short fuse, and small metal shards. A precursor to grenades, used by sappers and assassins.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Damage:<CharStyle:> Heavy · <CharStyle:Bold>Weight:<CharStyle:> 1.5 lbs · <CharStyle:Bold>Cost:<CharStyle:> 40 gp each · <CharStyle:Bold>Range:<CharStyle:> 30 ft (thrown)
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Traits:<CharStyle:> Explodes on 2-second fuse after thrown. Shrapnel deals damage in a 10-foot radius. Handle with care <0x2014> premature fuse burns have killed many thrower.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>The Flame Projector (Cheng-Huang)
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A Chinese experimental weapon: a portable pump-action incendiary sprayer, functionally similar to a small Greek Fire siphon but oil-based. Used by specialist military engineers; never widely deployed.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Damage:<CharStyle:> Heavy (fire) + continuing fire · <CharStyle:Bold>Range:<CharStyle:> 30 ft · <CharStyle:Bold>Weight:<CharStyle:> 20 lbs · <CharStyle:Bold>Cost:<CharStyle:> 800 gp
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Traits:<CharStyle:> Pump requires both hands. Fuel reservoir holds 10 shots. Reservoir can be set on fire if struck by fire attack (Major damage to wielder).
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000E>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Fantasy Variants
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Rune-Lock Firearm
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>Any firearm with a rune-bound firing mechanism instead of powder-and-priming. The weapon fires a bolt of elemental energy rather than a lead ball; damage type varies with the bound rune. Never misfires regardless of weather. Does not require powder; charges are built into the runes and recharge over 24 hours with light/moon/sun exposure as appropriate.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Cost:<CharStyle:> +Severe (×10) over base firearm. The mechanism itself requires Chapter 19 enchantment.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Dragon-Forged Cannon
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A heavy artillery piece cast from dragon-bone and steel, typically a culverin or bombard. The dragon-bone imparts elemental qualities to the shot <0x2014> fire-drake cannons fire incendiary shot, frost-drake cannons fire shot that freezes on impact, etc.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Cost:<CharStyle:> +Severe over base cannon.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Traits:<CharStyle:> The elemental damage is an additional Heavy amount applied to the cannon's normal damage.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Powder-Warded Arsenal
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>A barrel or chest of black powder treated with alchemical wards against accidental ignition. Safe from sparks and ordinary fire; only direct enchantment or alchemy can set off warded powder.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Cost:<CharStyle:> +Major over unwarded powder.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody><CharStyle:Bold>Traits:<CharStyle:> Immune to misfire-related chain explosions. Valuable for shipboard magazines and field magazines in active combat zones.
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Safety, Training, and the Gunpowder Economy
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
