<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading1>Appendix A: System Conversion Guide
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>How to Use This Appendix
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>The Three Armor Families
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarHeading>Which Style Is Mine?
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>If your game uses an <CharStyle:Bold>Armor Rating<CharStyle:> as a target number and tracks armor damage separately from personal damage, you are Style A.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>If your game expresses armor as a descending or ascending <CharStyle:Bold>Armor Class<CharStyle:> that affects to-hit rolls and has no armor-damage mechanic, you are Style B.
<ParaStyle:Sidebars:SidebarBody>If your game subtracts <CharStyle:Bold>Armor Points<CharStyle:> from every damage roll, you are Style C.
<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
