<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>16<0x2013>30
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Rotted food, bloodstained rags, broken gear.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>31<0x2013>50
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Small stash: 1d6 × 10 gp in mixed coin, 1d4 items from Chapter 14.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>51<0x2013>70
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Working camp supplies: tent, cooking gear, 2d6 days rations, 1d4 weapons.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>71<0x2013>85
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Leader's stash: 1d6 × 50 gp, quality weapon, valuables worth 50-200 gp.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>86<0x2013>93
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Stolen goods: 1d6 × 100 gp worth of trade goods (wool, salt, etc.).
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>94<0x2013>97
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Prisoner(s) or kidnapping victim. GM implications.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>98<0x2013>99
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>A sealed document implicating a local noble or official.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>100
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>A legendary piece (often stolen from a recent campaign).
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Monster Slain
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Roll
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Result
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>1<0x2013>60
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Harvestable materials only (see Ch 3 harvesting).
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>61<0x2013>80
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Prior victim's gear partially intact nearby.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>81<0x2013>90
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Accumulated shiny objects (raven-type hoard): 1d4 × 20 gp of small valuables.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>91<0x2013>97
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Significant kill's gear: full kit of 1 adventurer (weapons, armor, gold).
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>98<0x2013>100
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Unique item attached to the creature's lair.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Roll
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Result
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>1<0x2013>20
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Personal gear and trinkets (50-100 gp worth).
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>21<0x2013>50
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Crude weapons + 1d6 × 10 gp + food stores.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>51<0x2013>75
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Quality weapons and armor (light-medium) + 1d6 × 50 gp.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>76<0x2013>90
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Tribal wealth: 1d6 × 200 gp + group valuables.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>91<0x2013>97
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Chieftain's hoard: 1d6 × 500 gp + masterwork item + slaves or prisoners.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>98<0x2013>100
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Unique: ancestral relic, captured legendary piece.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Roll
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Result
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL><0x2014>
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>GM-designed hoard. Use Ch 19 framework. A dragon's hoard is a campaign event, not a random roll.
