<ParaStyle:Body Text:CoreBody><0x000C>
<ParaStyle:Headings:Heading2>Road Hazards
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Roll
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_HEADER>Encounter
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>1-60
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Nothing significant.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>61-70
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Another traveler or small caravan. Typically friendly; may share news.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>71-80
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Weather event (heavy rain, storm, blizzard) <0x2014> slows travel.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>81-88
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Bandit scouts observing from cover. Attack on a future day unless driven off.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>89-93
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Bandit attack. Strength scaled to caravan size.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>94-96
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Toll or checkpoint (legal or illegal). Requires payment or parley.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>97
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Broken bridge or washed-out road; detour required.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>98
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Sick or dying traveler requests help.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>99
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Lost child or lost wagon of another caravan seeking help.
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>100
<ParaStyle:Table:TABLE_CELL>Something truly strange (GM discretion <0x2014> unusual creature, lost ruin, magical event).
